# ${name}

A console application on the xtr packages.

## Run

```sh
uv run ${name}                  # every command
uv run ${name} app:hello Ada    # the example command
uv run ${name} debug:bundles    # the bundles and whether each is active
```

The environment is read from `.env`, then `.env.local`, then `.env.<APP_ENV>` and
`.env.<APP_ENV>.local`; a variable set in the shell wins. Keep machine-specific values in
`.env.local`, which is not committed.

## Layout

```
src/${app}/
├── __main__.py        the console entry point
├── kernel.py          the kernel every entry point builds, and the environment loader
├── config/
│   ├── bundles.py     the active bundles — written by xtr-recipes
│   └── packages/      one @configure module per bundle
└── command/           the console commands
```

## Add a package

```sh
uv run xtr-recipes recipes:add xtr-messenger
```

It installs the package and applies its recipe — the bundle, its configuration file, its
environment variables — and prints any step left to do by hand. `xtr.lock` records what was
applied; commit it.

## Check

```sh
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check && uv run ruff format --check
uv run basedpyright && uv run ty check
uv run xtr-recipes recipes:sync --check
```
